ELGAMAL & SCHNORR DIGITAL SIGNATURE
VARIABLE + PUBLIC/PRIVATE PARAMETER CHEAT SHEET

============================================================
ELGAMAL
============================================================

p
Name: Prime modulus
Meaning: Prime number used for modular arithmetic.
Status: PUBLIC

g
Name: Generator
Meaning: Generator/base used in modular exponentiation.
Status: PUBLIC

private_key
Math notation: x
Name: Private key
Meaning: Secret key of the signer.
Status: PRIVATE — MUST NOT be shared.

public_key
Math notation: y
Name: Public key
Meaning: y = g^x mod p.
Status: PUBLIC — can be shared.

k
Name: Random/ephemeral signing value
Meaning: Temporary value used to create a signature.
Status: SECRET during signing — do not reveal or improperly reuse.
In this lab code: k = 61 (hardcoded only for demonstration).

h
Name: Hash value / message digest
Meaning: SHA-256(message), reduced modulo (p-1) in this code.
Status: DERIVED value, not a secret.

k_inverse
Name: Modular inverse of k
Meaning: k^(-1) mod (p-1), used in the signature equation.
Status: SECRET/INTERMEDIATE value.

r
Name: First signature component
Meaning: r = g^k mod p.
Status: PUBLIC as part of the signature.

s
Name: Second signature component
Meaning: s = k^(-1)(h - x*r) mod (p-1).
Status: PUBLIC as part of the signature.

message
Name: Message
Meaning: Data being digitally signed.
Status: Usually PUBLIC in a signature-only scenario.

signature
Name: Digital signature
Meaning: The pair (r, s).
Status: PUBLIC.

ElGamal key relationship:
    x = private key
    y = public key = g^x mod p

Signing:
    h = H(message) mod (p-1)
    r = g^k mod p
    s = k^(-1)(h - x*r) mod (p-1)

Signature:
    (r, s)

Verification:
    y^r * r^s = g^h (mod p)

Parameters in THIS code:
    PUBLIC:  p = 467, g = 2
    PRIVATE: private_key = 127
    SECRET:  k = 61 (temporary signing value)


============================================================
SCHNORR
============================================================

p
Name: Prime modulus
Meaning: Prime number used for modular arithmetic.
Status: PUBLIC

q
Name: Subgroup order / prime-order parameter
Meaning: Parameter used for Schnorr calculations and modulo q.
Status: PUBLIC

g
Name: Generator
Meaning: Generator used for modular exponentiation.
Status: PUBLIC

private_key
Math notation: x
Name: Private key
Meaning: Secret key of the signer.
Status: PRIVATE — MUST NOT be shared.

public_key
Math notation: y
Name: Public key
Meaning: y = g^x mod p in this code.
Status: PUBLIC — can be shared.

k
Name: Random/ephemeral signing value
Meaning: Temporary value used during signing.
Status: SECRET during signing — do not reveal or improperly reuse.
In this lab code: k = 5 (hardcoded only for demonstration).

r
Name: Commitment / first signature component
Meaning: r = g^k mod p.
Status: PUBLIC as part of the signature.

e
Name: Challenge
Meaning: e = H(message + str(r)) mod q in this code.
Status: DERIVED/PUBLIC.

s
Name: Response / second signature component
Meaning: s = k + x*e mod q.
Status: PUBLIC as part of the signature.

message
Name: Message
Meaning: Data being digitally signed.
Status: Usually PUBLIC in a signature-only scenario.

signature
Name: Digital signature
Meaning: The pair (r, s).
Status: PUBLIC.

Schnorr key relationship:
    x = private key
    y = public key = g^x mod p

Signing:
    r = g^k mod p
    e = H(message || r) mod q
    s = k + x*e mod q

Signature:
    (r, s)

Verification:
    g^s = r * y^e (mod p)

Parameters in THIS code:
    PUBLIC:  p = 23, q = 11, g = 2
    PRIVATE: private_key = 3
    SECRET:  k = 5 (temporary signing value)


